      "fix_rationale": null,
      "ground_truth_root_cause": "The keystone charm's config-changed-postupgrade hook (run by the openstack-upgrade action)\ncalls update_all_domain_backends(), which calls domain_backend_changed() for every\ndomain-backend relation (e.g. keystone-ldap). domain_backend_changed() unconditionally calls\ncreate_or_show_domain(), which queries the local Keystone admin API through manager.py.\nUnlike the charm's other identity-relation hooks, domain_backend_changed() had no\nis_unit_paused_set() guard around that call. When the documented paused-single-unit upgrade\nprocedure pauses the keystone unit before running the openstack-upgrade action, the local\nKeystone API (served by apache2 on the admin port) is down, so the API call raises a\nConnectionRefusedError/RuntimeError and the hook crashes, breaking the procedure whenever a\ndomain-backend relation is present.",
      "unsupported_specifics": null,
